],"description_full":"FrontView REIT, Inc. is an internally managed net-lease real estate investment trust. It is focused on acquiring, owning, and managing properties with frontage that are leased to a diversified tenant base. Our real estate first investment strategy is centered around highly visible properties in prominent retail corridors with strong underlying real estate fundamentals. We target properties along high-traffic roads that offer strong consumer visibility and adaptable building formats capable of supporting various businesses over time. As of June 30, 2026, FrontView owned a diversified portfolio of 316 direct frontage properties across 35 U.S. states, leased primarily to service and necessity-based tenants across 16 industries, including medical and dental providers, quick-service and casual dining restaurants, financial institutions, cellular retailers, automotive related, fitness, and general retail along with several other diversified industries. FrontView REIT, Inc. is based in Dallas, United States and incorporated in Maryland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Drew M. Ireland | Chief Operating Officer | Age 46 | Compensation: $689,973 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 22 people. Revenue per employee of $3.1M ranks in the above the sector median among Real Estate peers. Stock-based compensation of $89K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["FrontView REIT, Inc. is a small-cap real estate business with a $607M market cap on $67M of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at -1% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 10.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -0.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 6.3% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 8600% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Real Estate peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 31% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Real Estate peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"FrontView REIT (NYSE:FVR) Stock Price Target Cut by JonesTrading","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/frontview-reit-nysefvr-stock-price-target-cut-by-jonestrading.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793972941.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.026,"tier":0,"scope":"c